{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage","id":1141843,"title":"Who is John Courage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-19T12:32:27-07:00","id":1141843,"title":"Who is John Courage?","content":"Is there anyone who can explain who John Courage is to me? He is mentioned in the books as an example character and discussed here occasionally but only in small detail. I saw mention of his profile being in The Digital Web, but he was not mentioned anywhere I could see. Is he still NWO or is he a different paradigm now? Is he in any novels or is he just a one time character. I am curious because he seems to be one of the few characters that is focused on between multiple books and the character is very interesting from the little amount I have seen. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16848-brassfist","name":"Brassfist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T14:43:29-07:00","id":1141903,"title":"","content":"There are actually lots of characters focused on between the books - as a matter of fact, each of the bright, colorful full-page artworks in M20 that show one or two characters? Those are recurring Mage characters. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Not all are equally presented between the books, but they are there - sometimes only in artwork, at other times in the book's intro/aftermath stories. Some even got their own Mage novels.<br /> <br /> The new M20 The Art Of Mage book actually talks about several of them.<br /> <br /> Hokay, John Courage.<br /> He is actually &quot;Secret Agent John Courage&quot; - and pretty much the quintessential &quot;Good Guy NWO&quot; icon character with a tragic past.<br /> He believes in the core mission statement of the Technocracy - help humanity, enlighten it and protect it - but is quite aware of the Technocracy's terrible faults.<br /> To such a degree that he sometimes actively secretly aids the Traditions, at other times aids Technocratic Amalgams. He's been a double agent, a triple agent, savior and friend of Lee Ann Miller (The Cult of Ecstasy icon character featured in a few books, including the M20 intro)...and he's a mess. The M20 intro hints at him having undergone quite a few visits to Room 101 in his time, but it never was enough to really break him. His past is utterly mixed up in his head however, unable to discern what of it is real and what of it is fabricated. His outward cold-as-ice behavior and combat training is NWO training through and through. He seems to be an expert at shielding his mind, and Lee Ann, despite being a powerful Cultist, states that he could utterly crush her if he wanted to.<br /> <br /> It's not quite clear why the Technocracy never really got rid of him - or what their official stance on him is in the M20 era, wether he is rogue or still officially part of the Convention. They used to be on the lookout, but it seems he now still pulls weight among the NWO - at least being able to call in favors, and he has access to the VDAS datacrawl - but why the Technocracy has left him alive compared to how some other people's transgressions have been dealt with is kind of a mystery. Perhaps he *has* a few secret friends in high places - perhaps even unknown to himself. That and he sort of is a literal icon among some Technocrats. The group &quot;The Friends of Courage&quot; is a secret cell within the Technocracy that tries to weed out the corruption that has shown itself here and there.<br /> <br /> Oh, and he's a powerful, enlightened badass.<br /> <br /> He gets mentioned in:<br /> <br /> Digital Web<br /> Hidden Lore<br /> Guide To The Technocracy<br /> Convention Book NWO (1st)<br /> Convention Book NWO (revised)<br /> M20 corebook<br /> M20 HDYDT intro - very worth it. Starts at the green VDAS output.<br /> <br /> And one, two other books, but only in mechanics examples, methinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-19-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T17:45:52-07:00","id":1141955,"title":"","content":"If you ever saw the list of &quot;pulp era&quot; Mage characters in Guide to the Traditions, there were supposed to have been Technocracy counterparts, with the original John Courage being the NWO signature, as an homage to period character Operator 5. (The others were homages to G-8, The Gladiator, Little Orphan Annie, and Flash Gordon.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T18:59:05-07:00","id":1141989,"title":"","content":"He's the rogue technocrat who breaks all the rules, but DAMN IT he gets results! He's a Technocracy urban myth given form. A living hyper narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-19T22:10:33-07:00","id":1142034,"title":"","content":"I suspect John Courage not being stopped by the Technocracy is a combination of several factors. First, like Ambrosia said, he probably has friends high up in the Union, both known and unknown to him. Some might see him as a necessary check to Union corruption (while providing a cover of plausible deniability), some might support him out of rivalry with other Union bigwigs, and others might have particular plans that factor Courage into, like a piece on a board.<br /> <br /> Second, and also like Ambrosia said, the common agents love him. He's too great an urban myth, as well as perversely a good morale booster. While the Union would probably like to be able to take him down - or at least leash him - they've seen what happens when a popular figure to Technocrats is eliminated. The Technocracy doesn't want to see a repeat of Alan Turing and the mass defection of the Virtual Adepts, or that onerous Luminiferous Ether fiasco. Who knows how heavily the NWO and other Conventions could fracture if an icon like John Courage was taken down. Especially if the Friends of Courage decide to team up with New Avalon, and demand that the Union reform or they all walk.<br /> <br /> Third, if John Courage were to be killed, he'd probably be replaced by someone else claiming to be Courage. For all the Union knows, that has happened several times already; the &quot;real&quot; John Courage having died long ago, and his crusade carried on by a series or even concurrent group of copycats and Courage worshipers. The man himself is almost besides the point; the real threat to the Union is his legend, and what it represents. A man can bleed, but ideas are bulletproof.<br /> <br /> Fourth - and perhaps most importantly - it's a bitch <i>finding</i> John Courage. There's a reason John Courage is directly referenced by M20 under the Arcane/Cloaking background. He's the quintessential man of mystery - a ghost in the system, whose resistance to being found is comfortably exceeded only by members of the Ahl-I-Batin. John Courage probably has Cloaking 5, which is at the level where it's difficult for even people who know him to remember who he is. Data about him is lost or corrupted, camera footage gets hazy, people fail to notice him unless he wants to be noticed. Even by some miracle witnesses recall his presence, they'd be hard pressed to tell you what he looked or sounded like. And all that is while he's not actively covering his tracks; this is just his passive cover provided by the background. As a master NWO operative, Courage is also augmenting that Cloaking with Mind, Forces, Matter, Entropy, Life, etc. Even if someone remembered his face, it's probably not the same face he wore last week. Assuming he even bothered to visit a location in person.<br /> <br /> And then you remember that he's a former Technocrat himself, and knows how the Union's surveillance operates. And if their methods change, he has enough Friends and backdoors that he can keep appraised of the latest updates. If John Courage didn't believe in the fundamental mission of the Technocratic Union, he'd be one of its most dangerous enemies. A man with a veritable knife to its underbelly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T03:30:41-07:00","id":1142086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1141903#post1141903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He believes in the core mission statement of the Technocracy - help humanity, enlighten it and protect it - (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Can this really be said at all to be the Technocracy's mission statement? After all, this mission statement of protect and enlighten is shared by <i>many </i>organizations, including many mundane human groups. Saying that this is the Technocracy's mission statement ignores their other core agendas, and the goals of the individual Conventions. And to me it feels like whitewashing the Technocracy, to an extent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T04:22:30-07:00","id":1142094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1142086#post1142086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can this really be said at all to be the Technocracy's mission statement? After all, this mission statement of protect and enlighten is shared by <i>many </i>organizations, including many mundane human groups. Saying that this is the Technocracy's mission statement ignores their other core agendas, and the goals of the individual Conventions. And to me it feels like whitewashing the Technocracy, to an extent.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is their core mission statement though. Always has been. Officially.<br /> <br /> It's the very precept the Order Of Reason was founded under back at the end of the Dark Ages - and they *were*, actually, the first global conspiracy to actually have that goal for the whole of mankind, instead of just their close environs or country.<br /> While everybody else was sticking to their own towers, trying to wage war aginst other countries, and not looking over the borders of their own fiefdoms, the Order Of Reason was thinking *big*. As in, *global*, wanted to protect humanity from the supernatural, fuel knowledge and scientific research, and pull humanity out of the dark and its lurking horrors into an age of enlightenment and technology. And that mission lasts to this day. Again...officially.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy nowadays has corrupt parts. Lots of them. The threat of internal civial war is brewing. It has done cruel, utterly horrible things in its crusades against the Traditions and the other supernaturals, and the sense of humanity and connection to the rest of mankind in many of its members is waning. The Schism between the frontline agents and Control, at least pre-Avatar-Storm, was getting huge.<br /> Which is exactly *why* people like John Courage, New Avalon, The Friends of Courage, Project Invictus and all the other Technocratic secret cells are actually trying to fight the corrupt elements, and restore the Technocracy to those old days of a more humane Order Of Reason, when it was helping mankind step up its game, And John Courage is a key figure in all that.<br /> <br /> I do not see the &quot;whitewashing&quot; you speak of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 09-20-2017, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T04:58:51-07:00","id":1142103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1142094#post1142094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is their core mission statement though. Always has been. Officially.<br /> (...)<br /> I do not see the &quot;whitewashing&quot; you speak of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stating that this - protect and help humanity - is their core mission statement misses the part when in the name of 'safety' they label and treat all that is non-scientific as something to be eliminated (and they aim to define what 'scientific' means). They call supernaturals &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; - including mystic True Mages. You might see someone like Secret Agent John Courage as one of the &quot;good Technocrats&quot; ; but from another perspective by remaining - even if partly - a Technocrat loyal to the Technocracy he is just another hostile human, and science, supremacist; the only difference with him is that he believes that his hands are clean.<br /> Constant repetition of the line that the Technocracy is about protecting humans carries an insidious implication that all the supernaturals and Nightfolk, that the Technocracy is trying to eliminate, pose a constant, unchangeable danger to humanity; which is not true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-20-2017, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T05:23:24-07:00","id":1142106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1142103#post1142103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stating that this is their core mission statement misses the part when in the name of 'safety' they label and treat all that is non-scientific as something to be eliminated (and they aim to define what 'scientific' means). They call supernaturals &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; - including mystic True Mages. You might see someone like Secret Agent John Courage as one of the &quot;good Technocrats&quot; ; but from another perspective by remaining - even if only partly - a Technocrat loyal to the Technocracy he is just another hostile human, and science, supremacist; the only difference with him is that he believes that his hands are clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't miss it. Mission statements are supposed to be ideals that a group holds in esteem. They are not a code of conduct or a complete philosophy. They are usually open ended, open to interpretation, and can be pursued in many more ways than the organization actually does. Groups frequently fail to live up to their ideals.<br /> <br /> Hell, the mission statement of Turing Pharmaceuticals is &quot;Dedicated to helping patients,who often have no effective treatment options, by developing and commercializing innovative treatments for serious diseases and conditions across a broad range of therapudic areas.&quot; That didn't stop them from buying the rights to a cheap decades old drug and raising the price over 5000%. <br /> <br /> Giving the Technocracy a noble mission statement does not ignore or paper over the terrible actions they've committed. Instead it gives them the tragedy and depth to be something other than moustache twirling villains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T09:00:50-07:00","id":1142175,"title":"","content":"Indeed. It's also worth to say that treating all that's &quot;non-scientific&quot; as something to be eliminated it's a relatively recent trend. Order of Reason had it's share of religious mystics and superstitionists. The Technocratic goal it's not so much a scientific world as &quot;One Truth, One Wolrd, One Reality&quot;, where that world it's safe and good for normal people...<br /> The high ups decided that this world it's one without monsters and ruled by scientific laws that can produce gadgets that everyone can use regardless of knowledge. If you think they're wrong about that, or if they are doing it wrong...well, no one said mages were infallible. Also, the majority of the Union was already working under scientific paradigm before they rejected the mystics, I think it made sense to have Sience as their &quot;One Reality&quot; to avoid internal conflicts, if nothing else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 09-20-2017, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T09:23:50-07:00","id":1142180,"title":"","content":"The Order of Reason has always been &quot;We will kill all the Unicorns if it gets rid of the dragons&quot;(Its right there in the opening fiction of Sorcerer's Crusade!). This does make them seem &quot;Bad' From the perspective of The Traditions and ESPECIALLY other game lines that do not consider humanity a priority(changeling, Werewolf. The more you allow other games to come into play the worse The technocracy looks). Now I would argue the plurality of paradigms in the Traditions proves the core ideal of &quot;One world One Reality&quot; as a necessity for human safety and development wrong but the position is one that can be held logically and consistantly.<br /> <br /> <br /> But that's drifting from what is John Courage. John Courage is a Legend. He's a Legend created by the hopes and dreams of every Technocrat who's had the system bite them in the ass. He's the hopes and dreams of every Sleeper who wants some bad ass guy out there protecting them. He is a mantle, a hypernarrative that people fall into. its why his memory and records are contradictory. Every time a John Courage dies a new one is born and subtle bends of reality make it so any proof of death was clearly false.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-21T09:58:51-07:00","id":1142572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1142103#post1142103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stating that this - protect and help humanity - is their core mission statement misses the part when in the name of 'safety' they label and treat all that is non-scientific as something to be eliminated (and they aim to define what 'scientific' means). They call supernaturals &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; - including mystic True Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The world can't hold all paradigms together. Not at he same strength anyway. The most saintly, most benevolent mage who does nothing but go around curing sick orphans is inadvertedly killing thousands, because each miraculous healing done weakens technocratic medicine that's used everywhere in the world these days.<br /> Traditions love to claim that everything can be a happy little hugbox where everyone just does whatever brand chaos magic they like, but they are yet to show this being the case. And the human price of even trying that would be astronomical.<br /> <br /> Back on topic. John Courage is a technocratic Big Good Gandalf NPC who is Better Than You, More Important Than You and is everything your whimpy little PC will never be. Like Shadowrun's Harlequin or Forgotten Realms' Elminster, Courage showing up means you should put down your dice and let the ST narrate exactly how John Courage one ups everything you'll ever do.<br /> I don't really like most White Wolf NPCs is what I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 09-21-2017, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:13:52-07:00","id":1144075,"title":"","content":"My personal take on John Courage that I plan on using for my games, regardless of what continuity says, is that -you- are John Courage. John Courage is a folk tale and myth, and the role has often been adopted by NWO Mages who are deep in quiet, as well as by other Mages of various factions. He's a superman, a boogey man, and a myth. The John Courage role is used by various Amalgams and Cabals who need plausible deniability. John Courage is dead, long live John Courage!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:16:50-07:00","id":1144077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144075#post1144075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take on John Courage that I plan on using for my games, regardless of what continuity says, is that -you- are John Courage. John Courage is a folk tale and myth, and the role has often been adopted by NWO Mages who are deep in quiet, as well as by other Mages of various factions. He's a superman, a boogey man, and a myth. The John Courage role is used by various Amalgams and Cabals who need plausible deniability. John Courage is dead, long live John Courage!</div> </div> </div> </div>Would explain his simple name and surname.<br /> <br /> You could have this, while also having an actual John Courage. Both him and the ones going into the role of John Courage could be unaware of the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:17:37-07:00","id":1144078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1142572#post1142572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The world can't hold all paradigms together. Not at he same strength anyway. The most saintly, most benevolent mage who does nothing but go around curing sick orphans is inadvertedly killing thousands, because each miraculous healing done weakens technocratic medicine that's used everywhere in the world these days.<br /> Traditions love to claim that everything can be a happy little hugbox where everyone just does whatever brand chaos magic they like, but they are yet to show this being the case. And the human price of even trying that would be astronomical.<br /> <br /> Back on topic. John Courage is a technocratic Big Good Gandalf NPC who is Better Than You, More Important Than You and is everything your whimpy little PC will never be. Like Shadowrun's Harlequin or Forgotten Realms' Elminster, Courage showing up means you should put down your dice and let the ST narrate exactly how John Courage one ups everything you'll ever do.<br /> I don't really like most White Wolf NPCs is what I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>How very Technocratic, saying that limitless Magick is scarce. No, the world *can* fit it all. Objective reality is a myth and the fear based paradigm of the Union has failed, as Capitalism is destroying the planet.<br /> <br /> The only limits are belief and will. Selfishness and fear are the chant of the Union and the Fallen, which is dooming the world. 90s cynicism kills fun in the game. Tragedy is ultimately failed storytelling.<br /> <br /> But, you are dead on with Courage. That's why Courage needs to be a mask and a myth any Mage can take.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:32:56-07:00","id":1144085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144078#post1144078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How very Technocratic, saying that limitless Magick is scarce. No, the world *can* fit it all. Objective reality is a myth and the fear based paradigm of the Union has failed, as Capitalism is destroying the planet.<br /> <br /> The only limits are belief and will. Selfishness and fear are the chant of the Union and the Fallen, which is dooming the world. 90s cynicism kills fun in the game. Tragedy is ultimately failed storytelling.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The whole argument of the Technocracy it's that believing in other things will weaken technology paradigm and we will get back to the dark ages. One could argue that the Traditions aren't about disbelieving in technology but about believing in other things too, and thus the Technocratic argument it's falacious, but reality being subjective or objective has nothing to do with it (humans would need to believe in everything the Traditions propose at once, if they can't or if they can't do so with enough strenght as to support &quot;mundane technology&quot;, then the Technocracy would be right).<br /> <br /> And about Courage, this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's the rogue technocrat who breaks all the rules, but DAMN IT he gets results! He's a Technocracy urban myth given form. A living hyper narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T08:44:00-07:00","id":1144087,"title":"","content":"I think the best take on John Courage is that he's actually a spirit created through the beleifs of the technocracy.<br /> <br /> He Fights corruption! Badass martial arts! He took the red pill! He's an amalgam of every badass secret agent, from the Prisoner to James Bond. He's a rogue agent! <br /> <br /> But he isn't real. Thats how he's still operating. He's a figment of mystical imagination thats been given so much strength because, no matter how much Technocrats repress their Avatar, they have to believe in something. <br /> <br /> All John Courage is an abnormally powerful spirit affected by belief. Which is why sometimes his backstory is contradictory and insane, his strength fluctuates.<br /> <br /> This way he can be used in the game without making him yet another &quot;schemer of schemers.&quot; Instead, he's the idealization of every technocrat, but also a reality deviant of the highest order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11894-shushu","name":"Shushu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T09:20:03-07:00","id":1144098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shushu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144087#post1144087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This way he can be used in the game without making him yet another &quot;schemer of schemers.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I imagine John Courage as a True Mage is more in line with Captain America from Marvel Comics, than a schemer. (though of course not really <i>like</i> Captain America). So strong tactical and strategical skills, keen wits, courage, and - of course - staying true to personal values. Consider that trying to do things, that are seemingly impassible because of how idealistic they are (or seem to be), can cause a person to develop just the means and reach such heights that those things become achievable.<br /> John Courage is also likely to be an expert at countering the efforts of those who try to exploit his idealism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-27-2017, 05:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T09:25:30-07:00","id":1144099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144078#post1144078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How very Technocratic, saying that limitless Magick is scarce. No, the world *can* fit it all. Objective reality is a myth and the fear based paradigm of the Union has failed, as Capitalism is destroying the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, what Technocracy proposes verifiably works. We can look at the history of the world in hundred or five hundred years and see how access to technology expanded human capabilities to do what previously was purely the domain of awakened magi. You can extrapolate this process to assume that at some point technocratic method will result in every human being able to perform feats of level 5 sphere magic.<br /> <br /> What Traditions are proposing is a pipe dream. They say that everyone can Ascend if they just believe. They say that Traditions can bring a magical hugbox where all paradigms are true and everyone is free to practice whatever brand of chaos magic they like. But what is this based on? Traditions sure as hell can't Awaken anyone right now and they don't even know what Ascension is like. If it's not a tug of war between paradigms, then what are Traditions fighting for? Why are they fighting the Technocracy at all instead of going full Taftani and showing all people all the magic all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 09-26-2017, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T09:34:07-07:00","id":1144102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144099#post1144099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, what Technocracy proposes verifiably works. We can look at the history of the world in hundred or five hundred years and see how access to technology expanded human capabilities to do what previously was purely the domain of awakened magi. You can extrapolate this process to assume that at some point technocratic method will result in every human will be able to perform feats of level 5 sphere magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until you turn the electricity off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T10:11:53-07:00","id":1144110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shushu</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best take on John Courage is that he's actually a spirit created through the beleifs of the technocracy.<br /> <br /> He Fights corruption! Badass martial arts! He took the red pill! He's an amalgam of every badass secret agent, from the Prisoner to James Bond. He's a rogue agent! <br /> <br /> But he isn't real. Thats how he's still operating. He's a figment of mystical imagination thats been given so much strength because, no matter how much Technocrats repress their Avatar, they have to believe in something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea. That would make Courage the counterpoint to Ascencion's take on Control. If Control it's the idealized &quot;hidden master&quot;, Courage would be the street agent that's free and gets things done. Like the guilty dream of Technocrats that acts as counterpoint to Control superego","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T19:12:37-07:00","id":1144253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144110#post1144110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting idea. That would make Courage the counterpoint to Ascencion's take on Control. If Control it's the idealized &quot;hidden master&quot;, Courage would be the street agent that's free and gets things done. Like the guilty dream of Technocrats that acts as counterpoint to Control superego</div> </div> </div> </div>Which feeds heavily into one of the themes first introduced in Guide to the Technocracy: the disconnect between the administration of the Union and the operatives standing on the Front Lines. The former represented by Control, a force supposedly perfect in its enlightened machine logic, and its understanding of the bigger picture; the latter represented by Courage, a man so focused on the simple act of defending Reality, regardless of the higher ups's priorities, that he's willing to be Deviant and &quot;unplugged&quot; (to borrow a term from Agent Smith) in order to get the job done.<br /> <br /> Both are exaggerated ideals, that Technocrats aspire to, but which they cannot (and probably <i>should not</i>) achieve fully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-26T19:30:15-07:00","id":1144257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144078#post1144078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How very Technocratic, saying that limitless Magick is scarce. No, the world *can* fit it all. Objective reality is a myth and the fear based paradigm of the Union has failed, as Capitalism is destroying the planet.<br /> <br /> The only limits are belief and will. Selfishness and fear are the chant of the Union and the Fallen, which is dooming the world. 90s cynicism kills fun in the game. Tragedy is ultimately failed storytelling.<br /> <br /> But, you are dead on with Courage. That's why Courage needs to be a mask and a myth any Mage can take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny. Magick is no more limitless than the men and women who are it's source. Humanity is the source of magick, and without Humanity then magick is nothing. The traditions seek to destroy the commonality of man in order to further their own selfish desire to shape reality to their whim. The Technocracy shapes reality for the betterment of all...<br /> <br /> And how do we know this? Because the Traditions had their time. They had their day. They shaped reality to their benefit and their benefit alone. Furthermore, the 'failings' of technocratic society are more often than not the result of the ongoing ascension war. As the traditions are as likely to slide 'facts' into the consensus as the Technocrats these days. Pollution, Global Warming... Heck, even car-sickness are the result of Traditional Willworkers laying curses into the Technocratic foundations. Why? Because they can't get over the fact that they lost. That the world they abused chose a better hope for the future.<br /> <br /> [Reminder: Report to Amalgam outpost 34-B for mandatory Psych Ops session following this encounter with a Superstitionist!]<br /> <br /> Will do ADEI, you're so handy. Reminding me to go to my brainwashing sessions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T02:02:13-07:00","id":1144314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1144257#post1144257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> And how do we know this? Because the Traditions had their time. They had their day. They shaped reality to their benefit and their benefit alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>When exactly did the Traditions have their time? The Traditions came together as a joint faction in response to the emergence of the Order of Reason. They never &quot;had their time&quot; as far as I'm aware of.<br /> <br /> <br /> By the way, to what extent were the belief and drive towards the Ascension of humanity present among True Mages before the founding of the Traditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-27-2017, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T06:23:23-07:00","id":1144366,"title":"","content":"Friendly reminder to all base personnel: Room 101 is for Mental Hygiene, not brainwashing. Those who cannot tell the difference should report to Room 101. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-27T07:37:03-07:00","id":1144401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, to what extent were the belief and drive towards the Ascension of humanity present among True Mages before the founding of the Traditions?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the Traditions like to use the word &quot;Ascencion&quot;, these ideals are very old. Enlightment that allows you to transcend reality was very present in the belief that form the foundings of many Traditions like the Akashicks and their legendary village of humble enlightened or the Hermetics with their, well, hermetic beliefs. The &quot;vision of ascencion&quot; than the Batini got was also received prior to the forming of the Traditions and it may as well be the real thing if we go by TOJ pseudo-canon. While not all Traditions are equally optimistic about the Ascencion of the masses, the idea that humans can Ascend was very present before the forming of the Council.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T00:38:13-07:00","id":1145994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1142103#post1142103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stating that this - protect and help humanity - is their core mission statement misses the part when in the name of 'safety' they label and treat all that is non-scientific as something to be eliminated (and they aim to define what 'scientific' means). They call supernaturals &quot;Reality Deviants&quot; - including mystic True Mages. You might see someone like Secret Agent John Courage as one of the &quot;good Technocrats&quot; ; but from another perspective by remaining - even if partly - a Technocrat loyal to the Technocracy he is just another hostile human, and science, supremacist; the only difference with him is that he believes that his hands are clean.<br /> Constant repetition of the line that the Technocracy is about protecting humans carries an insidious implication that all the supernaturals and Nightfolk, that the Technocracy is trying to eliminate, pose a constant, unchangeable danger to humanity; which is not true.</div> </div> </div> </div>And we are all aware of most of supernatruals and Nightfolk are evil and harmful to humanity. Nephandi are just one of infinite variants of evil, nefarious monsters prey on innocent humanity.<br /> <br /> Order of Reason and the Technocracy already destroyed threats of dragons, trolls, mythic monsters, fae folks, demons, spirits and shapeshifters prey on humanity. Now only the those bloodsucking parasites and Wyrm-Nephandi are left.<br /> <br /> It is our duty to end such atrocity.<br /> <br /> Let the Second Inquisition burns them all with purging flame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 10-02-2017, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T02:11:23-07:00","id":1146002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1145994#post1145994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And we are all aware of most of supernatruals and Nightfolk are evil and harmful to humanity. Nephandi are just one of infinite variants of evil, nefarious monsters prey on innocent humanity.<br /> <br /> Order of Reason and the Technocracy already destroyed threats of dragons, trolls, mythic monsters, fae folks, demons, spirits and shapeshifters prey on humanity. Now only the those bloodsucking parasites and Wyrm-Nephandi are left.<br /> <br /> It is our duty to end such atrocity.<br /> <br /> Let the Second Inquisition burns them all with purging flame.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are the Fera 'destroyed' ?<br /> <br /> What about the True Mages of the Traditions? What is the stance of the 'second inquisition' on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T02:23:03-07:00","id":1146005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146002#post1146002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are the Fera 'destroyed' ?<br /> <br /> What about the True Mages of the Traditions? What is the stance of the 'second inquisition' on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fera once oppressed, exploited and brutalized humanity as cattle, as the <i>Shattered Dream</i> attests crystal clear. Their tyranny over humankind was even crueler than vampires. But compared to their glory days, Fera are nearly gone extinct, their entire power base forever utterly broken.<br /> <br /> They could not become rulers or threat to humanity ever again. Unfortunately, they have never learned from their past debacles and determined to erase human civilization through enacting the &quot;Second Impergium&quot;<br /> <br /> So be it. Humanity is no longer powerless, we are not flocks to be herded anymore, regardless what the Beasts likes to imagine.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition is a Technocratic front, and secretly supported by Pentex(to exterminate Fera), but their stance regarding True Mages is unclear yet. Perhaps the Union is at the peace with Traditions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 10-02-2017, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T02:46:31-07:00","id":1146007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146005#post1146005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Second Inquisition is a Technocratic front, and secretly supported by Pentex(to exterminate Fera), (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this official? (And if yes, where can I read about it?) I thought they were supposedly independant mundane humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T02:51:19-07:00","id":1146008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146007#post1146007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this official? (And if yes, where can I read about it?) I thought they were supposedly independant mundane humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it appears they are tied with both the Technocracy AND Pentex.<br /> <br /> You can read it here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017/page3\">World of Darkness Berlin, 2017</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","user":"Numinous","date":". 10-02-2017, 05:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4173-numinous","name":"Numinous","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T06:30:00-07:00","id":1146041,"title":"","content":"&quot;...that all the supernaturals and Nightfolk, that the Technocracy is trying to eliminate, pose a constant, unchangeable danger to humanity; which is not true.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't understand how anyone could read any of the game lines in WoD and come away with this impression. Sure, some specific individuals may not pose a threat to humans, but the various supernatural groups as a whole are dangerous. The technocratic ideal of protecting humanity from the evils of deviants didn't spring up from nowhere. These games are about playing monsters and villains. <br /> <br /> Going back to John Courage, he represents the positive aspects of the Union and is a champion of humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T06:49:50-07:00","id":1146042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Numinous</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146008#post1146008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, it appears they are tied with both the Technocracy AND Pentex.<br /> You can read it here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017/page3\">World of Darkness Berlin, 2017</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Seems weird. Pentex is definitely not a group which would help this New Inquisition accomplish any of it's goals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T07:08:22-07:00","id":1146048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146041#post1146041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;...that all the supernaturals and Nightfolk, that the Technocracy is trying to eliminate, pose a constant, unchangeable danger to humanity; which is not true.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> I don't understand how anyone could read any of the game lines in WoD and come away with this impression. Sure, some specific individuals may not pose a threat to humans, but the various supernatural groups as a whole are dangerous. The technocratic ideal of protecting humanity from the evils of deviants didn't spring up from nowhere. These games are about playing monsters and villains. <br /> <br /> Going back to John Courage, he represents the positive aspects of the Union and is a champion of humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bleedover from IRL politics mostly. Most see the Union like the republican party given super science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T07:43:36-07:00","id":1146055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Most see the Union like the republican party given super science.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly White Wolf does. If the rumors I've seen are correct, The Technocracy was very much against the refugees , pretty much in line with Trump foreign policy (if not with all of it) in the 5th edition mage fiction. Which I think it's a bad way to portray them (I could understand that they don't like the &quot;superstitionists&quot; among foreigners, be them mage or mundane, but it just doesn't make sense because the Union's agenda it's global, they can't hide behind a frontier)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T08:12:23-07:00","id":1146062,"title":"","content":"Making the Union anti-immigration is definitely a bad idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13562-lordmagnusen","name":"lordmagnusen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T09:54:13-07:00","id":1146080,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy would definitely push for more globalist policies. Their ideals work best in a more unified world that has less contrast between the borders of various countries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T10:44:05-07:00","id":1146099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146080#post1146080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Technocracy would definitely push for more globalist policies. Their ideals work best in a more unified world that has less contrast between the borders of various countries.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. One World, One Truth, One Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T14:40:13-07:00","id":1146165,"title":"","content":"The issue here is that Technocracy is built on the US conspiracy lore. US conspiracy lore is very reactionary and right-wing; evil bankers running the world, evil secret societies running government, evil scientists, evil academics teaching cultural marxism, etc. Different conventions represent this: the Syndicate, the NWO, Iteration X, the Progenitors, and the NWO again. This runs into idiosyncrasies when mixed with Mage's anti-science stance and the punk idea of schools being brainwashing facilities, leading to the NWO controlling academia. Academia IRL has a strong tendency towards the left. If you're on the right, the horrible leftist academia and their critical theory cultural marxism is a clear sign of their participation in the Zionist conspiracies. But MTAs has to try to paint the NWO's control of leftist academia as actually being a right-wing plot. Which is strange.<br /> <br /> Things get even more weird when you move outside the US and have to represent foreign governments with stances opposite to the US' right wing as all being in on the Technocratic plot. Take European Union for example. In theory it is controlled by the Technocracy. In practice this means that either German technocrats are pro-immigration and globalization and British technocrats are anti-immigration and globalization and there's a civil war, or that Germany and the core EU are not controlled by the Technocracy. Because their government stance is opposite to the right-wing US stance.<br /> <br /> And then it all gets even worse when you have to talk about Technocratic China or Technocratic Saudi Arabia or Technocratic Singapore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 10-02-2017, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-02T16:34:11-07:00","id":1146187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146165#post1146165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue here is that Technocracy is built on the US conspiracy lore. US conspiracy lore is very reactionary and right-wing; evil bankers running the world, evil secret societies running government, evil scientists, evil academics teaching cultural marxism, etc. Different conventions represent this: the Syndicate, the NWO, Iteration X, the Progenitors, and the NWO again. This runs into idiosyncrasies when mixed with Mage's anti-science stance and the punk idea of schools being brainwashing facilities, leading to the NWO controlling academia. Academia IRL has a strong tendency towards the left. If you're on the right, the horrible leftist academia and their critical theory cultural marxism is a clear sign of their participation in the Zionist conspiracies. But MTAs has to try to paint the NWO's control of leftist academia as actually being a right-wing plot. Which is strange.<br /> <br /> Things get even more weird when you move outside the US and have to represent foreign governments with stances opposite to the US' right wing as all being in on the Technocratic plot. Take European Union for example. In theory it is controlled by the Technocracy. In practice this means that either German technocrats are pro-immigration and globalization and British technocrats are anti-immigration and globalization and there's a civil war, or that Germany and the core EU are not controlled by the Technocracy. Because their government stance is opposite to the right-wing US stance.<br /> <br /> And then it all gets even worse when you have to talk about Technocratic China or Technocratic Saudi Arabia or Technocratic Singapore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the same organization that backed both sides of WW2 to experiment on which societal model panned out better.<br /> <br /> You're presuming they have any sense of loyalty to the nation's they control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T00:52:33-07:00","id":1146275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146187#post1146187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the same organization that backed both sides of WW2 to experiment on which societal model panned out better.<br /> <br /> You're presuming they have any sense of loyalty to the nation's they control.</div> </div> </div> </div>So is Technocracy pro-immigration or anti-immigration? What is their stance on Brexit? Loyalty to the nation was not a question here at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 10-03-2017, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T01:30:17-07:00","id":1146277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146275#post1146275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is their stance on Brexit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's possible that Technocrats don't care, in a way. Some of them might have a preferred option - but whatever occurs they will make the their moves, and carry on as usual. It is very likely that all in all, compared to what the Technocracy does and how it functions, all that events like Brexit do is change <i>how</i> Technocrats will go about accomplishing their goals, rather than <i>what</i> goals they will be able to accomplish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-03-2017, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T02:15:30-07:00","id":1146283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146277#post1146277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's possible that Technocrats don't care, in a way. Some of them might have a preferred option - but whatever occurs they will make the their moves, and carry on as usual. It is very likely that all in all, compared to what the Technocracy does and how it functions, all that events like Brexit do is change <i>how</i> Technocrats will go about accomplishing their goals, rather than <i>what</i> goals they will be able to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't answer the question. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12710\" data-vbnamecard=\"12710\">PazuzuAxelf</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> posited that Technocracy is pro-globalism and pro-immigration. If that is the case, then what's going on in the UK? Did Technocrats lose control of the government? Have the british Technocats gone rogue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T05:08:41-07:00","id":1146298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146283#post1146283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't answer the question. <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> and <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> posited that Technocracy is pro-globalism and pro-immigration. If that is the case, then what's going on in the UK? Did Technocrats lose control of the government? Have the british Technocats gone rogue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if you want to pull from IRL influences as well as game...<br /> <br /> The Taftani own the middle east more or less. The richest parts of it are their plaything. Therefore, the refugee crisis is caused by the Taftani infiltration of the refugees.<br /> <br /> So, they're trying to keep their operations in Britain secure for the moment while still setting them up to fail and be reabsorbed later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T06:28:47-07:00","id":1146312,"title":"","content":"You can explain Brexit however you want, because obviously there's no official WoD answer to that as it's quite recent. There doesn't have to be any sort of supernatural conspiracy behind it at all if you don't want there to be. Just because something in real life occurred in a way that does not fit within their goals doesn't mean the Technocracy is not going to push for globalist policies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-03T12:19:54-07:00","id":1146409,"title":"","content":"Moreover, we must always remember that no supernatural conspiracy in the World of Darkness actually controls the governments of the world. To have the level of influence that they can stop this or that from happening would make said conspiracies too big to hide, and too all-powerful to fight. And it's been established that while the Technocracy is powerful, it likes everyone (who knows of it, anyway) to think it is greater, more cohesive, and more influential than it really is.<br /> <br /> Simply put, the Technocracy can't just counter every act of politics they may disagree with. Especially in a western democracy, where there is the presumption of transparency. In the case of Brexit, there was popular enough discourse about the UK leaving the EU that a vote was called for. And the Brexit went through because there was enough popular support for it from the UK's voter base (and/or enough apathy among those who might have opposed it or been ambivalent) to have it go through. If the Technocracy tried to stop the vote or alter the result, it would require a level of interference that might have tipped their hands to the public or regulatory agencies.<br /> <br /> The Union cannot have sleepers at large realizing its existence, so it tends to stay out of high profile democratic processes. Or at least it does so when the processes involve the public directly, rather than elected officials (who, naturally, can be bought and sold with relative impunity).<br /> <br /> Further, the Union may have been just as surprised by Brexit going through as the rest of the world. They didn't think they'd NEED to step in, even if they could or wanted to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T22:58:00-08:00","id":1186951,"title":"","content":"N-n-n-necro!!!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've always preferred a kind of weird interpretation of the TU, shameless Technocratic apologist that I am. Namely, that they would be considered paragons of progressive political policy and human rights. Maybe with a few skeletons in their closet, sure, but what organization can exist in some form for 500+ years and not have a few of those? But regardless, the Technocrats would be genuinely some of the most enlightened, progressive, open-minded and forward-thinking people you could possibly want to meet...<br /> <br /> If they had had the good fortune of being born in the real world. Unfortunately, they live in the world of Mage, where all the pie-in-the-sky dreams about faith healing and perpetual motion are actually totally possible. They live in a fantasy world with real world expectation. They're villains because they dismiss outlandish things as &quot;unrealistic&quot; and try to stop them from getting out and &quot;getting everyone's hopes up&quot;. Both the Techs and the Trads want the best for humanity, the difference is that the Techs think it's irresponsible and dangerous to rush things and the Trads want it <b>right now!</b><br /> <br /> So yeah, about as far from &quot;the GOP with hypertech&quot; as you can get, if you don't mind my political leanings coloring my interpretation.<br /> <br /> I also make psionics and about 80% of alien related stuff purely Etherite territory, because to me having them acknowledge stuff like that takes away from their themes of &quot;realistic progress versus childlike enthusiasm and fantasy&quot; and turns it into a slightly more unpleasant (for me) &quot;fun spiritualism versus boring technology&quot;. Of course, they get <i>some </i>ET action, because otherwise the Void Engineers would be pretty pointless, but I digress...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 02-17-2018, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:19:00-08:00","id":1186953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186951#post1186951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">N-n-n-necro!!!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've always preferred a kind of weird interpretation of the TU, shameless Technocratic apologist that I am. Namely, that they would be considered paragons of progressive political policy and human rights. Maybe with a few skeletons in their closet, sure, but what organization can exist in some form for 500+ years and not have a few of those? But regardless, the Technocrats would be genuinely some of the most enlightened, progressive, open-minded and forward-thinking people you could possibly want to meet...<br /> <br /> If they had had the good fortune of being born in the real world. Unfortunately, they live in the world of Mage, where all the pie-in-the-sky dreams about faith healing and perpetual motion are actually totally possible. They live in a fantasy world with real world expectation. They're villains because they dismiss outlandish things as &quot;unrealistic&quot; and try to stop them from getting out and &quot;getting everyone's hopes up&quot;. Both the Techs and the Trads want the best for humanity, the difference is that the Techs think it's irresponsible and dangerous to rush things and the Trads want it <b>right now!</b><br /> <br /> So yeah, about as far from &quot;the GOP with hypertech&quot; as you can get, if you don't mind my political leanings coloring my interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Syndicate members I'd meet if they existed IRL would be any of those things, but generally I'd assume the rest would be broadly more progressive. They would majoritively be smug atheist though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:26:51-08:00","id":1186956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186953#post1186953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Syndicate members I'd meet if they existed IRL would be any of those things, but generally I'd assume the rest would be broadly more progressive. They would majoritively be smug atheist though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, but I've always gotten the impression that the rest of the Union thinks that way about the Syndicate too and keeps them around as a necessary evil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:36:20-08:00","id":1186957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186956#post1186956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> True, but I've always gotten the impression that the rest of the Union thinks that way about the Syndicate too and keeps them around as a necessary evil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like there are poles. &quot;Big Brother is our Friend&quot; and &quot;Hunger drives Innovation!&quot; with syndicate largely at one end even though they hypocrically have no issue with manipulating the market, and the NWO being at the other with the other three having degrees of &quot;Money is a Hastle&quot; and &quot;I'm a post human entity of course I can get whatever I want&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:43:22-08:00","id":1186958,"title":"","content":"I guess everyone else found the Atlas Shrugged jokes too obvious to bother with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:45:57-08:00","id":1186960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186957#post1186957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I feel like there are poles. &quot;Big Brother is our Friend&quot; and &quot;Hunger drives Innovation!&quot; with syndicate largely at one end even though they hypocrically have no issue with manipulating the market, and the NWO being at the other with the other three having degrees of &quot;Money is a Hastle&quot; and &quot;I'm a post human entity of course I can get whatever I want&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perhaps, but the social darwinism and classism the Syndies demonstrate is probably not something the rest of the Union is into. I probably don't have to explain why the NWO and the Progs aren't huge fans of it, ItX wants <i>everyone </i>to be a cool immortal machine man and the VE's are too busy fighting for the masses to give philosophies that divide humanity against itself the time of day. Like I said, necessary evil. (And I suspect that even the Syndicate hedge closer to libertarianism than actual honest-to-god neoreactionary social conservatism.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-16T23:51:17-08:00","id":1186961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1146409#post1146409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the Technocracy tried to stop the vote or alter the result, it would require a level of interference that might have tipped their hands to the public or regulatory agencies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main worry of Technocrats in such situations is making themselves visible and exposing themselves to, for example, Kindred, Traditions Mages, or Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 02-17-2018, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T00:39:13-08:00","id":1186972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186960#post1186960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Perhaps, but the social darwinism and classism the Syndies demonstrate is probably not something the rest of the Union is into. I probably don't have to explain why the NWO and the Progs aren't huge fans of it, ItX wants <i>everyone </i>to be a cool immortal machine man and the VE's are too busy fighting for the masses to give philosophies that divide humanity against itself the time of day. Like I said, necessary evil. (And I suspect that even the Syndicate hedge closer to libertarianism than actual honest-to-god neoreactionary social conservatism.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think the platform is as universal for the progenitors and IX. I think there are probably a signficant amount of Progenitors and Ixers who.. don't give a fuck, who are all in for their personal transcendence into a cool immortal machine, or would have no issue with instituting Brave New World style class system, or who buy into the &quot;We have earned our Technology, I'm not giving it away&quot;<br /> <br /> So I'd see them hedging towards libertarianism, but have no problem using neoreactionaries to get there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T00:46:40-08:00","id":1186975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186972#post1186972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think the platform is as universal for the progenitors and IX. I think there are probably a signficant amount of Progenitors and Ixers who.. don't give a fuck, who are all in for their personal transcendence into a cool immortal machine, or would have no issue with instituting Brave New World style class system, or who buy into the &quot;We have earned our Technology, I'm not giving it away&quot;<br /> <br /> So I'd see them hedging towards libertarianism, but have no problem using neoreactionaries to get there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That definitely does account for some members. That said, in light of the Revised Conbooks, I think the overall party line leans much less in that direction.<br /> <br /> Regardless, I think the idea of the Union being anti-refugee is pretty ridiculous, bordering on designated villain territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":12001,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","user":"The Nilbog","date":". 02-17-2018, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T04:27:31-08:00","id":1187006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186975#post1186975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That definitely does account for some members. That said, in light of the Revised Conbooks, I think the overall party line leans much less in that direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying this in light of Revised Progenitors, there is a huge split between the people who want to save the world, the people who have no problem wasting resources making monsters, and those who have &quot;grown up&quot; about money.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Regardless, I think the idea of the Union being anti-refugee is pretty ridiculous, bordering on designated villain territory. </div> </div> </div>Well.. the Union are designated villains, maybe not on the Nephandi level and there are shades of grey and nuance and alot of good intentions to them but they are designated villains.<br /> <br /> Now them being anti-refugee does seem to be fairly inconsistant with their portrayal in the revised books, but the Technocracy has been shown to be more than willing to break ALOT of eggs to make delicious omlets. So while i don't think they'd follow reactionary nationalism(They want the One world Government, they have a Convention called &quot;The New World Order&quot;...) using it as part of a larger plan isn't outside bounds.<br /> <br /> M20 also sort of wanted to say the Union had been coopted by the Nephandi so.. that too might make sense...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T09:00:53-08:00","id":1187054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187006#post1187006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well.. the Union are designated villains, maybe not on the Nephandi level and there are shades of grey and nuance and alot of good intentions to them but they are designated villains.</div> </div> </div> </div>Call me crazy, but I think they can still be antagonists without being designated villains. The trick is to keep them internally consistent and have well-defined boundaries on their goals and methods. Brainwashing Reality Deviants? Sure. Stoking the flames of xenophobia such that innocent sleepers are hurt in the crossfire? That's crossing a line. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187006#post1187006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 also sort of wanted to say the Union had been coopted by the Nephandi so.. that too might make sense...</div> </div> </div> </div>Not huge on that idea. M20 made very few changes to the setting that I liked and that was not one of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T11:44:29-08:00","id":1187098,"title":"","content":"Also: as of M20, Technocrats aren't even the designated antagonists anymore. Sure, they <i>can</i> be; but there's a reason why the Conventions are specced up in exactly the same way as the Traditions and why the book takes so many pains to enable not just technomancer protagonists, but Technocratic protagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T11:46:46-08:00","id":1187102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187098#post1187098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: as of M20, Technocrats aren't even the designated antagonists anymore. Sure, they <i>can</i> be; but there's a reason why the Conventions are specced up in exactly the same way as the Traditions and why the book takes so many pains to enable not just technomancer protagonists, but Technocratic protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that definitely <i>was </i>a change I can get behind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-17T13:18:51-08:00","id":1187127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187054#post1187054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Call me crazy, but I think they can still be antagonists without being designated villains. The trick is to keep them internally consistent and have well-defined boundaries on their goals and methods. Brainwashing Reality Deviants? Sure. Stoking the flames of xenophobia such that innocent sleepers are hurt in the crossfire? That's crossing a line.<br /> <br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> <br /> Not huge on that idea. M20 made very few changes to the setting that I liked and that was not one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is a common misconception: that the Technocracy has one policy.<br /> <br /> Despite the rethoric the Conventions are very different one from another. What is true for the Void engineers is not true for the NWO. Ask a Void Engineers what does he think about NWO, they will probably prefer having buisness with traditions (and they do).<br /> <br /> There is a wide range of morality, where the Void Engineers are the best guys, Iteration X and the Progenitors stand in the middle, and the NWO and the Syndicate are the worst of the lot, each one for different reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187054#post1187054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Brainwashing Reality Deviants? Sure. Stoking the flames of xenophobia such that innocent sleepers are hurt in the crossfire? That's crossing a line.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point. For the Void engineers even the brainwashing part would be bad. And for sure they would not put innocent sleepers on the crossfire, they would find it repulsive. The NWO? Well, that's another story.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even the policy regarding reality deviants is different. For a Void Engineers the Euthanatos are not only not dangerous for mankind, but even allies. On the other side a Vampire in a engineer's eyes is good only for target practice. For a NWO mage an Euthanatos is worst than most, while a vampire could be a political partner.<br /> <br /> Progenitors view on the Vampires<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The NWO point of view on vampires is the Technocratic party line: no open hostility as long as they keep their so-called Masquerade up. We\u2026 disagree. Looking at the facts should convince any rational scientist that there is no room for leniency. Vampires feed on the Masses. Vampires are not only a contagion, but also a powerful and secret culture. They create through a bodily process a highly addictive substance, known as \u201cvitae.\u201d They\u2019re vectors for mundane plagues. Worst, a sizeable faction does not care for operating in secret, causing as much memetic damage as biological. </div> </div> </div>and then the Syndicate<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires are interesting case studies. On one hand, they represent functioning anachronism in a microcosm: their secret society is based on feudalism, while they interact with our modern economy. It\u2019s a stable system, one that makes dealing with vampires relatively easy as long as their \u201cMasquerade\u201d is not threatened. On the other hand, some of their longer-lived ilk have entrenched themselves in Consensual economy. Honestly, it\u2019s hard not to respect the power that comes from being able to invest in an institution for decades or even centuries \u2014 though don\u2019t mistake that respect for vampiric reverence overall. With those Reality Deviants, we can strike peaceful accords. Money is, after all, the lingua franca of society, and even vampires can value peace and profitable business. With the younger or more rebellious of their kind, though, that\u2019s best left to other Conventions to exterminate. Not that we can\u2019t, but our Enforcers are better served protecting the Bottom Line, and there are a bunch of overzealous Progenitors who would be happy to slaughter brutish leeches. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So one should never speak about the Technocracty as ONE entity, that's the party line, in truth they are so different at their core that they are on the verge of civil war.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even the control freak fascist attitude, it depends. Void Engineers and Syndicate are not on that boat. NWO and Progenitors on the other hand...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 02-17-2018, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-18T06:19:38-08:00","id":1187271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187006#post1187006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 also sort of wanted to say the Union had been coopted by the Nephandi so.. that too might make sense...</div> </div> </div> </div>Correction: this idea is pitched as an *optional* choice for the Storyteller to use if they want to portray the Union in the classic style of the first two editions of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T15:32:53-08:00","id":1188320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187098#post1187098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: as of M20, Technocrats aren't even the designated antagonists anymore. Sure, they <i>can</i> be; but there's a reason why the Conventions are specced up in exactly the same way as the Traditions and why the book takes so many pains to enable not just technomancer protagonists, but Technocratic protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue M20 continues to present The Technocracy as antagonists. Especially to Technocrats.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1187271#post1187271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correction: this idea is pitched as an *optional* choice for the Storyteller to use if they want to portray the Union in the classic style of the first two editions of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea is pitched as part of &quot;canon&quot; for the Disparate Alliance. There's also some stuff that's leaked out there about NuWhitewolf direction including Technocracy going wildly reactionary which... if they were fully coopted by the Nephandi would make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T15:43:30-08:00","id":1188321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1188320#post1188320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The idea is pitched as part of &quot;canon&quot; for the Disparate Alliance. There's also some stuff that's leaked out there about NuWhitewolf direction including Technocracy going wildly reactionary which... if they were fully coopted by the Nephandi would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also undoes 2 1/2 decades of work to make the Technocrats more nuanced and sympathetic, turning them into political strawmen whose practices don't even remotely align with their aesthtic or stated ideals. It would be like having an aristocracy-controlled Southern militia in the 1800s start advocating for socialism. Sure, they're fictional, so you can have them advocate for whatever you want, but there's a definite thematic disconnect when academia, medicine, NASA and Silicon Valley are all portrayed as radically conservative reactionary institutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:00:36-08:00","id":1188385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1188320#post1188320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea is pitched as part of \u201ccanon\u201d for the Disparate Alliance. There's also some stuff that's leaked out there about NuWhitewolf direction including Technocracy going wildly reactionary which... if they were fully coopted by the Nephandi would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ParaWolf stuff isn't canon <i>yet</i>. As for M20, it makes a point to say that Nephandic infiltration of the Technocracy is <i>not</i> certain; and as far as the Disparates are concerned, it matters more that they <i>believe</i> that the Nephandi are pulling the Technocracy's strings than whether the Nephandi <i>actually are</i> pulling the Technocracy's strings. This is combined with a bit of Storyteller advice to the effect of \u201ckeep the players guessing whether or not the Technephandi are real or a paranoid delusion.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-21T20:04:19-08:00","id":1188387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1188321#post1188321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also undoes 2 1/2 decades of work to make the Technocrats more nuanced and sympathetic, turning them into political strawmen whose practices don't even remotely align with their aesthtic or stated ideals. It would be like having an aristocracy-controlled Southern militia in the 1800s start advocating for socialism. Sure, they're fictional, so you can have them advocate for whatever you want, but there's a definite thematic disconnect when academia, medicine, NASA and Silicon Valley are all portrayed as radically conservative reactionary institutions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; this is one reason why I personally prefer what M20 calls the \u201ckinder and gentler Technocracy\u201d, and why assuming that they're the designated villains and so needn't have any redeeming qualities rubs me the wrong way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-22T22:53:50-08:00","id":1188784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1186951#post1186951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">N-n-n-necro!!!<br /> <br /> Anyway, I've always preferred a kind of weird interpretation of the TU, shameless Technocratic apologist that I am. Namely, that they would be considered paragons of progressive political policy and human rights. Maybe with a few skeletons in their closet, sure, but what organization can exist in some form for 500+ years and not have a few of those? But regardless, the Technocrats would be genuinely some of the most enlightened, progressive, open-minded and forward-thinking people you could possibly want to meet...<br /> <br /> If they had had the good fortune of being born in the real world. Unfortunately, they live in the world of Mage, where all the pie-in-the-sky dreams about faith healing and perpetual motion are actually totally possible. They live in a fantasy world with real world expectation. They're villains because they dismiss outlandish things as &quot;unrealistic&quot; and try to stop them from getting out and &quot;getting everyone's hopes up&quot;. Both the Techs and the Trads want the best for humanity, the difference is that the Techs think it's irresponsible and dangerous to rush things and the Trads want it <b>right now!</b><br /> <br /> So yeah, about as far from &quot;the GOP with hypertech&quot; as you can get, if you don't mind my political leanings coloring my interpretation.<br /> <br /> I also make psionics and about 80% of alien related stuff purely Etherite territory, because to me having them acknowledge stuff like that takes away from their themes of &quot;realistic progress versus childlike enthusiasm and fantasy&quot; and turns it into a slightly more unpleasant (for me) &quot;fun spiritualism versus boring technology&quot;. Of course, they get <i>some </i>ET action, because otherwise the Void Engineers would be pretty pointless, but I digress...</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that if that was true, their would be no conflict between the Traditions and the Technocracy. In fact, if the Technocracy embraced modern progressive thought and dropped their whole cultural imperialism schtick aganist other cultures and beliefs, they'd be kissing the ass of the Dreamspeakers and apologizing for being asshats centuries ago. Instead, they still actively shun them because of vague notions of their magic being unrealistic, which is only true because the Technocracy manipulated the Consensus and the Sleepers to be that way. <br /> <br /> I have nothing aganist this idea, to be honest, but it would eliminate the most interesting antagonists in Mage and it badly clashes with the Technocracy's actually actions. It's kind of weird to claim to be progressive and open-minded when you still disregard so-called unrealistic things that you know can work with some effort is all I'm saying. Really, a progressive Technocracy would just be a more organized Society of Ether, embracing any possible avenue towards human improvement, which could mean anything from cybernetics to shamanism. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T06:53:35-08:00","id":1188857,"title":"","content":"Except shamanism, and other mystical beliefs, have no foundation in science. They're altruistic about advancing humanity through science. The entire point of their structure is to unite humanity into one belief system to achieve mass ascension. Diversity hinders this and has spawned a variety of responses from individual Technocrats. Unfortunately some of those responses were rather extreme - such as using mind control and labeling non-conformist as Reality Deviants. <br /> <br /> The Technocracy is not a complete lost cause. They're not all villains. They have goodness within them but just like the Traditions they have made mistakes. They are fundamentally human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:05:31-08:00","id":1188889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1188784#post1188784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem with this is that if that was true, their would be no conflict between the Traditions and the Technocracy. In fact, if the Technocracy embraced modern progressive thought and dropped their whole cultural imperialism schtick aganist other cultures and beliefs, they'd be kissing the ass of the Dreamspeakers and apologizing for being asshats centuries ago. Instead, they still actively shun them because of vague notions of their magic being unrealistic, which is only true because the Technocracy manipulated the Consensus and the Sleepers to be that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Realism has nothing to do with why the Technocracy opposes the Dreamspeakers. They oppose them because the Union believes their animistic beliefs are actively dangerous and unhelpful to Sleepers.<br /> <br /> What the Technocratic Union wants is not just a unified Reality, but a <i>standardized</i> Reality. They want a Reality governed by natural laws. Laws that can be measured, codified, and exploited. The Union wants a reliable Reality. What they emphatically DO NOT want is a Reality where mankind's ability to manipulate their environment is held hostage to the whims of alien intelligences from another dimension. That is a Reality where humans must live in thrall to invisible beings that share none of humanity's values and interests, when they aren't outright parasitic to humanity.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the next point: if the Consensus allows spirits to exist, it also allows BAD spirits to exist, and to affect the material world. And remember, the more people accept the idea of a spirit world, the thinner the barrier is between that world and ours. If everyone believed in an animistic worldview, the Gauntlet, if it existed at all, would be paper thin. Allowing all the blasphemous abominations from beyond reality to freely run roughshod over Earth and its people. Allowing Bygones to stride the land, unfettered and powerful and <i>hungry</i>. Allowing even the weakest of malignant ghost or bane to terrorize and attack and <i>mutate</i> the innocent.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union opposes the Dreamspeakers because the Union has an entire Convention devoted to matters on the other side of the Gauntlet. And those Void Engineers have nothing but horror stories to tell about the Umbra, and why it needs to be kept well the hell away from mundane Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 02-23-2018, 02:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T09:40:03-08:00","id":1188902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1188889#post1188889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Realism has nothing to do with why the Technocracy opposes the Dreamspeakers. They oppose them because the Union believes their animistic beliefs are actively dangerous and unhelpful to Sleepers.<br /> <br /> What the Technocratic Union wants is not just a unified Reality, but a <i>standardized</i> Reality. They want a Reality governed by natural laws. Laws that can be measured, codified, and exploited. The Union wants a reliable Reality. What they emphatically DO NOT want is a Reality where mankind's ability to manipulate their environment is held hostage to the whims of alien intelligences from another dimension. That is a Reality where humans must live in thrall to invisible beings that share none of humanity's values and interests, when they aren't outright parasitic to humanity.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to the next point: if the Consensus allows spirits to exist, it also allows BAD spirits to exist, and to affect the material world. And remember, the more people accept the idea of a spirit world, the thinner the barrier is between that world and ours. If everyone believed in an animistic worldview, the Gauntlet, if it existed at all, would be paper thin. Allowing all the blasphemous abominations from beyond reality to freely run roughshod over Earth and its people. Allowing Bygones to stride the land, unfettered and powerful and <i>hungry</i>. Allowing even the weakest a malignant ghost or bane to terrorize and attack and mutate the innocent.<br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union opposes the Dreamspeakers because the Union has an entire Convention devoted to matters on the other side of the Gauntlet. And those Void Engineers have nothing but horror stories to tell about the Umbra, and why it needs to be kept well the hell away from mundane Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is reason why I've never been able to really like the Technocracy, and why I wish they were more like the Society of Ether/VAs, or at least actually resembled what The Nilbog what's them to be. Pretending that the Dreamspeakers paradigm demands that humanity be utterly subservient to the will of alien spirits is a bastardization of their actual beliefs of mutual cooperation and understanding of spirits, many of which actually share humanistic beliefs and morals. Furthermore, the Technocracy being paranoid about Bad spirits is hypocritical when you consider that Science allows for the existence of bad things as well from nukes to mustard gas. And humanity being under the thrall of &quot;natural laws&quot; that were really created by the scientists of the Order of Reason and later on the Technocrats still threatens human agency as they create arbitrary limits that aren't in anyway inherently benign to humanity as whole. And lastly there's the whole slandering, brainwashing and murdering non-Technocrat mages for the crime of preaching their paradigm because doing so MIGHT hypothetically destroy the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 02-23-2018, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T10:03:40-08:00","id":1188909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1188902#post1188902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is reason why I've never been able to really like the Technocracy, and why I wish they were more like the Society of Ether/VAs, or at least actually resembled what The Nilbog what's them to be. Pretending that the Dreamspeakers paradigm demands that humanity be utterly subservient to the will of alien spirits is a bastardization of their actual beliefs of mutual cooperation and understanding of spirits, many of which actually share humanistic beliefs and morals. Furthermore, the Technocracy being paranoid about Bad spirits is hypocritical when you consider that Science allows for the existence of bad things as well from nukes to mustard gas. And humanity being under the thrall of &quot;natural laws&quot; that were really created by the scientists of the Order of Reason and later on the Technocrats still threatens human agency as they create arbitrary limits that aren't in anyway inherently benign to humanity as whole. And lastly there's the whole slandering, brainwashing and murdering non-Technocrat mages for the crime of preaching their paradigm because doing so MIGHT hypothetically destroy the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these things are why the Technocracy is flawed, and where drama comes from. Both as something to be opposed by Tradition and Craft mages, and internally as a problem its own members must grapple with.<br /> <br /> Of course the Dreamspeakers aren't advocating complete subservience to the spirit world. That's an inherent limitation of the Technocracy, in that their world view does not think highly of any Paradigm that doesn't put humanity first. That, however, is also baked into the Technocracy's inherently humanist worldview.<br /> <br /> Moreover, their worldview is inherently cynical, paranoid, and untrusting. While every other mage group looks at their personal worldviews and sees the positive aspects, the Union sees its dangers. Their view is extreme, sure, but they have a point. If Dreamspeakers succeeded in thinner the Gauntlet and allowing man and spirit to interact, it would by definition also make it easier for malign spirits to do so. And while every Dreamspeaker will claim that it's okay, because THEY are there to keep the peace and balance, the Technocracy isn't as confident in the abilities of the shaman and medicine person to do so. After all, the Order of Reason was around in an earlier age, where spirits were believed in fully. They SAW how well that turned out, and would rather not go back to those times.<br /> <br /> This does not excuse the Technocracy's actions, no. They ARE extreme, ARE taking their point too far, ARE corrupt. That is all true. But it's also interesting in a morally complex way. Especially in light of the presence of Technocrats within the organization that wish for reform. In this way, I DON'T think the Technocracy should just be like the Etherites or the Virtual Adepts. The Union as it is provides ground for the telling of unique stories. In that manner, I'd glad that there are many different ways the idea of Science and Technology can be explored in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T10:22:24-08:00","id":1188919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1141843-who-is-john-courage?p=1188902#post1188902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is reason why I've never been able to really like the Technocracy, and why I wish they were more like the Society of Ether/VAs, or at least actually resembled what The Nilbog what's them to be. Pretending that the Dreamspeakers paradigm demands that humanity be utterly subservient to the will of alien spirits is a bastardization of their actual beliefs of mutual cooperation and understanding of spirits, many of which actually share humanistic beliefs and morals. Furthermore, the Technocracy being paranoid about Bad spirits is hypocritical when you consider that Science allows for the existence of bad things as well from nukes to mustard gas. And humanity being under the thrall of &quot;natural laws&quot; that were really created by the scientists of the Order of Reason and later on the Technocrats still threatens human agency as they create arbitrary limits that aren't in anyway inherently benign to humanity as whole. And lastly there's the whole slandering, brainwashing and murdering non-Technocrat mages for the crime of preaching their paradigm because doing so MIGHT hypothetically destroy the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what makes the Technocracy such intriguing antagonists. They're the definition of the road to Hell is paved with good intentions. On the surface they seem very on point, but just following the logical conclusion of their goals would be terrifying. We're not going to end up in Startrek and Starwars with these guys.<br /> <br /> At least to me the Technocracy isn't really about science. It's not about making the world a better place. It's about making the world a <i>safer</i> place, which includes keeping humanity from making those 'unsafe' choices. This is control. You want the wonders of Tony Stark, Shuri, Mythbusters type of 'Get in losers, we're doing SCIENCE!&quot; that's the Etherites, Vadepts, and even individual members of the Conventions. The Technocracy as a whole, and to the members of the Inner Circle, not a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T10:47:31-08:00","id":1188928,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;Traditions want to get back to the dark ages&quot; it's propaganda. What it isn't propaganda it's the original purpose of the Order of Reason, which they have been mostly able to achieve, that it's to allow humans to use magic in order to get power for themeselves in a World of Gods and Monsters where humans are the bottom of the foodchain. As Onkwe stated, this was to create a safer world <i>for </i>humans (they weren't really that fixated on making it safer <i>from </i>humans, though)<br /> <br /> The Craftmasons put humans in a methapysical pedestal, they were the first to trully bend over themselves to provide magical power to the uninitiated, the common man. While they didn't invented science, they sure as hell defended and opened their research, increasing a lot the speed of human development. Freeing magical power over the masses at a much greater rate than anyone would have dared.<br /> <br /> The Traditions, for all their lofty ideals of freedom, are inherently elitist - Dreamspeakers, for instance, never have hidden that it's THEIR responsability, the Shamans place, to mediate between the Spirit and the Flesh. Hermetics sure do teach their stuff and put humans in a pedestal (unsurprisingly, the branch didn't fall THAT far from the tree) - but they won't allow the unenlightened to see the mysteries.<br /> Merely working hard it's not enough for them, you need to &quot;get it&quot;, you need to be one of the few Chosen, you need to achieve that state that's the stuff of mystical initiations, Awakening or at least Sorcery, both rare states that are granted by an occult source.<br /> Modern Traditions aren't better: Etherites are Geniuses that know better and VA won't accept anyone that doesn't &quot;get it&quot; as well as they do. I wouldn't like to see *their* definition of &quot;user friendly&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> While the Traditions won't cause humanity to get back to the Dark Ages nor revoque the actions of the Craftmasons, they wouldn't have left the Dark Ages by themselves (albeit I think that humans could have managed, given time), they just don't have an approach to magick that translates well to Joe Average using it.<br /> Technocracy fostered that line of tought, and latter young Traditionalists tought: Man, maybe spreading out tools isn't a bad idea, this tech stuff it's great. They're very democratic now but they're still quite fixated on the idea of lenghty initiations and secret knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-23-2018, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T11:05:51-08:00","id":1188933,"title":"","content":"That's part of the main theme of Mage. Ascension is not something that can be standardized, there is not Ascension101. So it is inevitable that the traditions lives on a individualistic voyage, it's the whole point of the Sphynx message: Enigma will take us where Dogma cannot. Ascension cannot be a product of Dogma, is a personal and inner struggle, the best thing that Traditions and Conventions can do is create a world were you have all the instruments to underake the journey, but in the end it will be all about you and your personal quest.<br /> <br /> At the same time Convetions are just as elitist as Traditions. Extraordinary citizens will never become true Technocrats, they lack enlightment, and Technocracy knows it. At the sime time is way easier for a young mage to get in contact with an archmage than for a Agent to get in contact with Control. White suits and Board Members do not spend time educating the young ones, they are not Senex or Porthos, the higher ups of the Technocracy are completely alien to the organization, and even more Technocracy is so elitist that only the highest rank of the pyramid knows that in the end Technocrats are mage too. There is no problem for the Conventions to spread use of the lastest Iphone, but knowledge? True knowledge with capital K? That's not for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 02-23-2018, 02:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-23T11:23:19-08:00","id":1188942,"title":"","content":"M20 describes Technocrats as the ultimate Alpha Testers: they get first crack at new inventions, decades before they're stable enough for the Masses. But a big part of their point is that what they're developing is being developed with an eye toward <i>making</i> it available to the Masses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}